<title>USA: TABLE - Tanger Factory Q2 net, share rise.</title>
<headline>TABLE - Tanger Factory Q2 net, share rise.</headline>
<dateline>GREENSBORO, N.C. 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>(In thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>					 3 Months Ended   6 Months Ended</p>
<p>						 June 30,	   June 30,</p>
<p>				 1997	 1996	 1997	 1996</p>
<p>Revenues</p>
<p>   Base rentals (a)   $13,710    $12,423    $26,958    $24,718</p>
<p>   Percentage rentals     305	  331	  703	  598</p>
<p>Expense reimbursements</p>
<p>				6,202	5,210     11,599     10,545</p>
<p>   Other income	     239	  225	  421	  451</p>
<p>   Total revenues     20,456     18,189     39,681     36,312</p>
<p>    Total expenses     16,599     14,598     31,859     28,811</p>
<p>Income before minority interest</p>
<p>and extraordinary item</p>
<p>				3,857	3,591	7,822	7,501</p>
<p>Minority interest (b)</p>
<p>			    (1,043)	(957)    (2,150)    (2,018)</p>
<p>Income before extraordinary</p>
<p>     item		   2,814	2,634	5,672	5,483</p>
<p>Extraordinary item -- Loss</p>
<p>on early extinguishment of debt,</p>
<p>net of minority interest of $270</p>
<p>				  --	   --	   --	 (561)</p>
<p>    Net income	  $2,814     $2,634	$5,672     $4,922</p>
<p>Per common share outstanding (c):</p>
<p>Income before extraordinary item</p>
<p>			     $0.34	$0.32	 $0.71	$0.67</p>
<p>     Net income	  $0.34	$0.32	 $0.71	$0.58</p>
<p>Funds from operations before</p>
<p>minority interest (d)</p>
<p>			    $8,431     $7,720     $16,633    $15,540</p>
<p>Funds from operations per</p>
<p>share (fully diluted) (e)</p>
<p>			     $0.79	$0.73	 $1.56	$1.47</p>
<p>    Average Shares 6,742,885  6,335,111   6,724,528  6,313,197</p>
<p>NOTES: (a)  Includes straight-line rent adjustment of $75 and $335 for three months ended, and $207 and $707 for six months ended June 30, 1997 and 1996.</p>
<p>(b)  Minority interest represents the original owners of the company's percentage ownership in the Operating Partnership during each period shown.</p>
<p>(c)  Income in per share computations are net of applicable preferred dividends.</p>
<p>(d)  Funds from operations is defined as income (loss) before extraordinary items and gains (losses) on sale of property, plus depreciation and amortization uniquely significant to real estate.</p>
<p>(e)  Assumes conversion of all preferred depositary shares to common shares as of January 1, 1996.  Not shown in income per share computations since the effect of conversion would be anti-dilutive.</p>
<p>Full co name is Tanger Factory Outlet Centers Inc.</p>
